# Cloudflare static-assets redirects. Copied into out/ by `next build`.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/
#
# 1. Finnish moved from /fi/ to the site root, English from / to /en/. These
#    keep every already-shared Finnish link working, permanently, so the move
#    costs nothing. Order matters: the first match wins.
/fi/tesla/   /tesla/     301
/fi/tesla    /tesla/     301
/fi/og.png   /og.png     301
/fi/         /           301
/fi          /           301

# 2. Without these, the asset server's own slash handling answers /tesla with a
#    307 — a TEMPORARY redirect, which tells Google to keep the slashless URL
#    around. Every page lives at its trailing-slash URL (trailingSlash: true),
#    so say so permanently.
/tesla       /tesla/     301
/en          /en/        301
/en/tesla    /en/tesla/  301

# 3. Google Search Console's verification file has to answer at its EXACT URL.
#    The asset server's html_handling drops ".html" and sends a 307 to the
#    extensionless path, and a verification file behind a redirect is not worth
#    risking. Status 200 here is a rewrite, not a redirect: the exact URL serves
#    the file's bytes. Keep this rule as long as the property is verified.
/googlef5fb86be7b72c0c2.html  /googlef5fb86be7b72c0c2  200
